=== talk-grange

--- start
GRANGE: "Nothing personal, ever — that's the first rule of this hallway." He offers macadamia candy from a tin. "Our members just want predictability. Tax bills are weather. We sell umbrellas."
POLICY BRAIN: Predictability IS worth money. He's the most honest person on this floor, in the way a price tag is honest.
TALK STORY: Take the candy. Audit the metaphor. Weather doesn't hire three lobbyists per raindrop.

* Take the candy. Keep walking.
  {}
  It's good candy. It is always good candy.
